## 🛣️ Routing Conventions

### Route Structure

```jsx
// src/services/providers/RouterProvider.jsx
const router = createBrowserRouter([
  {
    path: "/",
    element: <Index />,
  },
  {
    path: "/auth/*",
    element: <RequireGuest />,
    children: [
      { path: "login", element: <Login /> },
      { path: "signup", element: <Signup /> },
      { path: "forgot-password", element: <ForgotPassword /> },
      { path: "reset-password/:token", element: <ResetPassword /> },
      { path: "verify-email/:token", element: <VerifyEmail /> },
    ],
  },
  {
    path: "/dashboard",
    element: <RequireAuth><Dashboard /></RequireAuth>,
  },
  {
    path: "/social",
    element: <RequireAuth />,
    children: [
      { path: "posts", element: <SocialPosts /> },
      { path: "analytics", element: <SocialAnalytics /> },
      { path: "scheduler", element: <SocialScheduler /> },
    ],
  },
]);
```

### Route Categories

| Prefix | Purpose | Guard Required | Example |
|--------|---------|----------------|---------|
| `/` | Landing page | None | `/` |
| `/auth/*` | Authentication | `RequireGuest` | `/auth/login` |
| `/dashboard` | Main dashboard | `RequireAuth` | `/dashboard` |
| `/social/*` | Social tools | `RequireAuth` | `/social/posts` |
| `/seo/*` | SEO tools | `RequireAuth` | `/seo/keywords` |
| `/ads/*` | Advertising | `RequireAuth` | `/ads/campaigns` |
| `/outreach/*` | Email outreach | `RequireAuth` | `/outreach/sequences` |
| `/admin/*` | Admin panel | `RequireAuth` + Admin | `/admin/users` |
| `/settings/*` | User settings | `RequireAuth` | `/settings/profile` |

### Adding a New Route

**Step 1**: Create the page component with lazy loading

```jsx
// src/ui/pages/Analytics/index.jsx
import { lazy } from 'react';
export const Analytics = lazy(() => import('./Analytics'));
```

```jsx
// src/ui/pages/Analytics/Analytics.jsx
