## 📝 Code Style & Best Practices

### General Rules

1. ✅ **Use functional components** - no class components
2. ✅ **Use hooks** for logic reuse
3. ✅ **Destructure props** for readability
4. ✅ **Use arrow functions** for consistency
5. ✅ **Add JSDoc comments** for complex functions
6. ✅ **Keep files under 300 lines** - split if longer
7. ✅ **Use early returns** to reduce nesting
8. ✅ **Prefer const over let** - immutability first
9. ✅ **Use template literals** for string concatenation
10. ✅ **Avoid unnecessary ternaries** - use early returns

### Code Examples: Good vs Bad

#### ❌ Bad Example

```jsx
function MyComponent(props) {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);
  
  useEffect(() => {
    fetch('/api/data').then(res => res.json()).then(d => setData(d));
  }, []);
  
  return (
    <div>
      {data ? (
        <div>
          {data.map((item) => (
            <p>{item.name}</p>
          ))}
        </div>
      ) : (
        <p>Loading...</p>
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Problems:**
- No error handling
- Uses .then() instead of async/await
- No loading state management
- No keys in list
- Props not destructured
- Nested ternaries

#### ✅ Good Example

```jsx
function MyComponent({ userId, onDataLoaded }) {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [error, setError] = useState(null);
  const { toast } = useToast();
  
  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchData = async () => {
      try {
        setLoading(true);
        const response = await fetch(`/api/data/${userId}`);
        
        if (!response.ok) {
          throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);
        }
        
        const result = await response.json();
        setData(result);
        onDataLoaded?.(result);
      } catch (err) {
        setError(err.message);
        toast({
          title: "Error",
          description: "Failed to fetch data",
          variant: "destructive",
        });
      } finally {
        setLoading(false);
      }
    };
    
    fetchData();
  }, [userId, onDataLoaded, toast]);
  
  // Early returns for different states
  if (loading) return <Spinner />;
  if (error) return <Alert variant="destructive">{error}</Alert>;
  if (!data || data.length === 0) return <EmptyState />;
  
  return (
    <div className="space-y-4">
      {data.map((item) => (
        <Card key={item.id}>
          <p className="font-medium">{item.name}</p>
        </Card>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Improvements:**
- Proper error handling
- Uses async/await
- Separate loading/error states
- Keys in list
- Props destructured
- Early returns
- Optional chaining for callback

